-- title:
--   From HTo GTail Stage Mass Cons Eq Adjacent Stage A0 Branch
-- statement:
--   **A fixed tail type mass is the corresponding adjacent A0 branch.** Let $\psi$ be the two-register state, let $F$ be the indexed polynomial family, let $\ell,n$ be natural numbers, let $b$ be a Boolean, and let $\tau$ be a G-hat type of length $n$. Write $S$ for the recurrence weight at the prepended type, let $\mathcal U$ be the product of the uniform distributions on $\mathbb{F}_q$ and length-$n$ point tuples, and write $U$ and $T$ for the indexed outcome and half-product operators. If $M$ denotes the tail-stage mass, then
--
--   $$
--   M(\operatorname{prepend}(b,\tau))
--   =\mathbb E_{(x,\mathbf x)\sim\mathcal U}\sum_{g,h}^{b,\tau}
--   \operatorname{ev}_\psi\!\left(L(UTT^\dagger U)R(S)\right),
--   $$
--
--   where the superscripted sum is filtered by the head flag $b$ and tail type $\tau$, and $L,R$ are the tensor placements. This is the branch-level bridge from recursive tail mass to the explicit adjacent-stage A0 expression.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGTailStageMass_cons_eq_adjacentStageA0_branch`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
